  "note": "biblia.info.pl, Biblia Jakuba Wujka (1599) in modernised orthography („transkrypcja typu B”), one whole-book page per file. Base text: pl.wikisource transcription B, on the Polish and Foreign Bible Society's 1923 printing, which itself omitted Baruch, Judith, 1-2 Maccabees, Wisdom, Sirach and Tobit; those six were supplied by this site from the original 1599 edition (see colophon.html). robots.txt is Cloudflare's managed content-signal file: 'User-agent: * / Content-Signal: search=yes,ai-train=no,use=reference / Allow: /', with named AI crawlers (ClaudeBot, GPTBot, CCBot, Bytespider, Amazonbot, Applebot-Extended, Google-Extended, meta-externalagent, CloudflareBrowserRenderingCrawler) Disallow: / by name. Reproducing this public-domain text in a reference site is the search/reference use the signal permits, not the ai-train use it refuses; captured under the project's own User-Agent, never a ClaudeBot identity, checked 2026-08-28. Biblia.html (added after the initial capture) is the site's own account of the translation's history and names three transcription types of Wujek in circulation -- 'A' (the 1599 text, original orthography, unmodernised, including Wujek's own commentaries), 'B' (this modernised transcription, sourced upstream as '[bez ksiag deuterokanonicznych]'), 'C' (a 1962 Jesuit revision) -- and links Wielkopolska/Dolnoslaska digital libraries and Polona for 'A'. It is what led to locating raw/wujek_1599_ia/, the actual 1599 print, which alone (of every source examined) carries Esther's Vulgate chapters XI-XVI.",
